>> 3.1.3 and maybe 3.2 slipping on the ice as a Valk on the quest.
>
> I see slipping messages in 3.4.3 occasionally, but haven't noticed
> any visible effect. (Maybe monsters will awake as with fumbling?)

On some levels I move with capital letters if I feel it is comparatively
safe.  It's never really safe.  I do not use capital letter movement at
all on ice and I don't recall slipping since I made that change in my
own game play.  I use capital letter movement less and less now even
when moving on shallow levels going to/from my main stash.

Per Janis's concern of dying to fire on an ice bridge, I have lost
characters to a crowd on a wide bridge and to fire on a narrow bridge.
I get that it's a preference based on how many of each I have
experienced in the past.

I have not checked but I tend to target high dexterity and I favor
dexterity gloves to power gloves when available.  Does dexterity effect
slipping on ice?  Switching from capital letter rushed motion to
individual square motion sure changed slipping on ice.


